{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-2414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-6t.$ \nAt time $t=2,$ the particle is located at the position $x=6.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-2414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =6+{\\int }_{2}^{5}(3{t}^{2}-6t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =6+{[{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =6+([(5)^{3}-3(5)^{2}]-[(2)^{3}-3(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =6+([125-75]-[8-12]) \\\\  & =6+(50-(-4)) \\\\  & =6+54 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=60.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-2414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c26d92fafc1f814abbcaca5a0a85a2115614efcb064bad32b3a553a21ffab29"} {"question" "q-2414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-2414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "52"] ["math" "56"] ["math" "60"] ["math" "68"] ["math" "79"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-2414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-7113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=4t+3{t}^{2}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=12.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-7113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =12+{\\int }_{1}^{4}(4t+3{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =12+[2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}]_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =12+([2(4)^{2}+{4}^{3}]-[2(1)^{2}+{1}^{3}]) \\\\  & =12+([32+64]-[2+1]) \\\\  & =12+(96-3) \\\\  & =12+93 \\\\  & =105\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=105.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-7113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c26d92fafc1f814abbcaca5a0a85a2115614efcb064bad32b3a553a21ffab29"} {"question" "q-7113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-7113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100"] ["math" "105"] ["math" "92"] ["math" "93"] ["math" "97"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-7113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "105"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/assets/e484bfde797b94d298227bac9ae25fb68a3de5698e7f8d8527e37e11cb051a95.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{8}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=1$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{8}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{8}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8)=1+14=15\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=15.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c26d92fafc1f814abbcaca5a0a85a2115614efcb064bad32b3a553a21ffab29"} {"question" "q-81510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "23"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/assets/6c0f74fa4820cd8e6945666ab90e0eafac4cc1ada7578fb5a053f197adf08084.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=2+0=2\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c26d92fafc1f814abbcaca5a0a85a2115614efcb064bad32b3a553a21ffab29"} {"question" "q-81515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-81515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-351449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=6t-{t}^{2}.$ At time $t=3$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=6.$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-351449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=3$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [3,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(3)+{\\int }_{3}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(6) & =2+{\\int }_{3}^{6}(6t-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{[3{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}]}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =2+[3(6)^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(6)^{3}]-[3(3)^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =2+36-18 \\\\  & =2+18 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-351449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c26d92fafc1f814abbcaca5a0a85a2115614efcb064bad32b3a553a21ffab29"} {"question" "q-351449" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"} {"question" "q-351449" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/state.json" "file_sha256" "57b120f8b7ee1e3b672a143d15afbb6c07833de3868af5a9272d48a29a20a2e4"}] "usage" {"q-7113" [] "q-81515" []} "basis" 1568 "retractions" [[17592186176479 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t > 0$ is given by $v(t) = 4t + 3t^{2}$. At time $t = 1$ the particle is located at the position $x = 12$. What is the position of the particle at time $t = 4$?"] [17592186176497 :question/problem "![](/home/jak